[
  {
    "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition features two simple, matte ceramic plates positioned side by side, with the foreground plate sharp and the background plate softly blurred. The camera angle is 3/4 overhead, capturing the full arrangement of the ingredients. On each plate, a generous dollop of smooth, beige traditional hummus is placed off-center, sprinkled with a fragrant dusting of brown and green za'atar seasoning. Beside the hummus, a crisp whole-grain crispbread is propped up against the side of the plate. Freshly sliced dark green English cucumber rounds and vibrant red cherry tomato halves are arranged neatly in distinct sections alongside the hummus. A small handful of raw, light-tan unsalted almonds are scattered naturally between the vegetables. A light drizzle of lemon juice adds a subtle, realistic sheen to the surfaces of the vegetables. The scene is set on a warm, weathered oak table with visible wood grain. Props include a wooden spoon resting casually next to the plates and a few stray za'atar flakes and a crumb trail on the wood surface, suggesting a freshly prepared snack. Soft natural light from a window on the left casts gentle, realistic shadows. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene is lived-in, warm, and authentic. Includes slight natural imperfections like an asymmetric garnish and uneven vegetable placement. No plastic sheen, no artificial symmetry, no hands or faces. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. Indistinguishable from a professional editorial food photograph for a high-end cookbook."
  }
]
